{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["The meaning of 'from strength to strength' — the journeys that the festal pilgrims make, from the root of חיל וחומה. The correct interpretation is that חיל is a company of many people, like a band of prophets, until they arrive at the place of glory in Zion; and the meaning is that each one of them will see, as in: 'to see the face of YHWH your Elohim.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 84, :notes {0 "Resolved לראות את פני ה' אלהיך as a paraphrase of Deuteronomy 16:16; the psalm verse itself reads יראה אל אלהים בציון (Psalms 84:8)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:00.258927189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}